# Reviewed species dossiers.
#
# The four AFP knowledge overlays (identification, behavior, diet, seasonal
# calendar) live in Supabase rather than in the client bundle. They are public
# reference data — `public.species_dossiers` carries a SELECT policy for the
# `anon` role gated on `published`, exactly like `species`, `waters` and
# `agencies`. Nothing here involves a sign-in, and no user data is read.
#
# Set both in Vercel (Project Settings -> Environment Variables) and in a local
# `.env` for `npm run dev`.
#
# Leaving them unset is safe. The overlay routes fall back to the same reviewed
# records committed under `data/dossiers/` and `src/lib/knowledge/*-dossiers.ts`
# — the very records `npm run db:seed-dossiers` pushes into Supabase — so a
# clean checkout renders the full species pages and the response says
# `source: "committed"` rather than `"live"`. What you lose without a key is the
# ability to publish a review without a deploy, which is the whole reason the
# records live in a database at all.
#
# Fill in the key before shipping a review cycle; do not fill it in just to make
# the app work.
SUPABASE_URL=https://bvjpbpjhddjeloeoghdd.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Write access, for `npm run db:seed-dossiers -- --write` only. This is the
# session pooler connection string from Project Settings -> Database. It is not
# needed to run the app, and must never be exposed to the client.
# DATABASE_URL=
